                           \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                                                                \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                                                    \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                                                                                                \n                    \n                                                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n                                                \n                        \n                        \n                                    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                                                    \n                    \n                        \n    \n    \n    \n        \n    \n\n    \n        \n                        \n        \n        \n                        \n\n        \n        \n        \n                \n                    \n                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    \n                                                \n                    \n                    \n    \n    \n        \n                \n                    \n                                    \n\n\n\t\t\n\n\n\n\n                                        <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! -->\n\n                \n<div itemprop=\"articleBody\" id=\"article-body\"><p>Gemini has fully replaced Google Assistant on Android Auto, introducing an intelligent co-pilot in your dashboard. It can transform your daily commute if you learn to use it smartly, though we've also seen    <span data-id=\"1036293\"><a href=\"/android-auto-users-are-convinced-gemini-makes-driving-more-dangerous/\" target=\"_blank\">users complain that Gemini on Android Auto makes driving less safe</a></span>.    </p>    <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><p>Regardless of whether you love it or not, Google is giving us all kinds of hints that Gemini on Android Auto is here to stay. Not only that, but Google is quietly working towards improving the Gemini experience on Android. And one of the first few things it's planned to do seems to be a design makeover.</p>    <p>As spotted by <a href=\"https://www.androidauthority.com/gemini-android-auto-new-animation-apk-teardown-3719046/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Android Authority</a>, Google is planning to introduce a new Gemini animation on Android Auto. The new animation was spotted in the latest version of the Android Auto app (v7.9.664004). </p>    <p>The new animation is still hidden, but folks over at Android Authority have managed to enable it on their devices, giving us a clear look at how it is different from the current one.</p>    <!-- No AdsNinja v10 Client! --><h2 id=\"upcoming-gemini-ui-in-android-auto-is-more-noticeable\">\n                        Upcoming Gemini UI in Android Auto is more noticeable\n               </h2>\n<p>Currently, Gemini's listening indicator is a small line of glowing blue light that appears at the bottom of the    <span data-id=\"1036625\"><a href=\"/how-use-an-old-phone-as-an-android-auto-display/\" target=\"_blank\">Android Auto interface</a></span>. But this will likely be replaced by the upcoming animation, where the glowing effect is more pronounced. Also, the animation now spans across the entire width of the screen, not a small portion, unlike the current UI.    </p>    \n                \n    \n    \n    \n                \n    \n                \n                \n                \n        \n                                                            \n                                                                                                                        \n                            \n    \n    \n\n    \n    <div data-img-url=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg\" data-modal-id=\"single-image-modal\" data-modal-container-id=\"single-image-modal-container\" data-img-caption=\"&quot;Android Authority&quot;\">\n                                                                                            <figure><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 480px)\" data-srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=500&dpr=2\" srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=500&dpr=2\">\n        <source media=\"(max-width: 767px)\" data-srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=800&dpr=2\" srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=800&dpr=2\">\n        <source media=\"(max-width: 1023px)\" data-srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=825&dpr=2\" srcset=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=825&dpr=2\">\n        <img width=\"1650\" height=\"928\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"Screenshot showing Gemini's upcoming UI in Android Auto\" data-img-url=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=825&dpr=2\" src=\"https://static0.anpoimages.com/wordpress/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/upcoming-gemini-ui.jpg?q=49&fit=crop&w=825&dpr=2\">\n        </picture><small>Credit:&#160;Android Authority</small></figure>\n            \n        </div>\n<p>This is part of Google's effort to revamp Gemini's UI using what the company calls Neural Expressive design language, which the company announced at its annual developer conference in May this year. So, the experiment isn't really surprising to us. In fact, we would be surprised if Google put this on the back burner.</p>    \n\n                \n<p>On top of this—and this one is quite surprising—Google is also working on a \"Personalization\" feature for Gemini on Android. Just like how it works on mobile phones, Gemini on Android Auto will also be able to respond with connected apps and past conversations, according to Android Authority. While the appeal won't be as much as on phones, it's the right move to make Gemini more personalized on Android Auto.</p>    <p>We haven't seen a hands-on demo of how the feature works in the real world, unlike the new animation. This suggests that the new animation could release sooner than the \"Personalization\" feature. Either way, we can't wait to use them to    <span data-id=\"1032466\"><a href=\"/this-is-the-simple-way-to-elevate-your-android-auto-experience/\" target=\"_blank\">elevate our Android Auto experience</a></span>.    </p>    \n    \n    \n    \n</div>\n    \n            \n                        \n                \n        \n        \n\n                    \n    \n                        \n    \n\n\n                                                                \n        \n        \n    \n\n        \n    </article>\n\n    \n            \n        </DIV></DIV>","content_text":"Published Oct 5, 2026, 8:31 AM EDT Sign in to your Android Police account Gemini has fully replaced Google Assistant on Android Auto, introducing an intelligent co-pilot in your dashboard. It can transform your daily commute if you learn to use it smartly, though we've also seen users complain that Gemini on Android Auto makes driving less safe. Regardless of whether you love it or not, Google is giving us all kinds of hints that Gemini on Android Auto is here to stay. Not only that, but Google is quietly working towards improving the Gemini experience on Android. And one of the first few things it's planned to do seems to be a design makeover. As spotted by Android Authority, Google is planning to introduce a new Gemini animation on Android Auto. The new animation was spotted in the latest version of the Android Auto app (v7.9.664004). The new animation is still hidden, but folks over at Android Authority have managed to enable it on their devices, giving us a clear look at how it is different from the current one. Upcoming Gemini UI in Android Auto is more noticeable Currently, Gemini's listening indicator is a small line of glowing blue light that appears at the bottom of the Android Auto interface. But this will likely be replaced by the upcoming animation, where the glowing effect is more pronounced. Also, the animation now spans across the entire width of the screen, not a small portion, unlike the current UI. Credit: Android Authority This is part of Google's effort to revamp Gemini's UI using what the company calls Neural Expressive design language, which the company announced at its annual developer conference in May this year. So, the experiment isn't really surprising to us. In fact, we would be surprised if Google put this on the back burner. On top of this—and this one is quite surprising—Google is also working on a \"Personalization\" feature for Gemini on Android. Just like how it works on mobile phones, Gemini on Android Auto will also be able to respond with connected apps and past conversations, according to Android Authority. While the appeal won't be as much as on phones, it's the right move to make Gemini more personalized on Android Auto. We haven't seen a hands-on demo of how the feature works in the real world, unlike the new animation. This suggests that the new animation could release sooner than the \"Personalization\" feature. Either way, we can't wait to use them to elevate our Android Auto experience.","fetched_at":"2026-10-06T12:10:54.368Z","ok":true,"blocks":[{"html_en":"<p><time datetime=\"2026-10-05T12:31:43Z\"><span>Published</span> Oct 5, 2026, 8:31 AM EDT</time>\n                        </p>","sentences":[{"en":"Published Oct 5, 2026, 8:31 AM EDT","zh":null}]},{"html_en":"<p>Sign in to your <span>Android Police</span> account</p>","sentences":[{"en":"Sign in to your Android Police account","zh":"登录您的 Android Police 帐户"}]},{"html_en":"<p>Gemini has fully replaced Google Assistant on Android Auto, introducing an intelligent co-pilot in your dashboard. It can transform your daily commute if you learn to use it smartly, though we've also seen    <span data-id=\"1036293\"><a href=\"/android-auto-users-are-convinced-gemini-makes-driving-more-dangerous/\